            <line x1="30" y1="70" x2="70" y2="70"/><line x1="30" y1="70" x2="50" y2="44"/><line x1="70" y1="70" x2="50" y2="44"/>
            <line x1="50" y1="44" x2="50" y2="16"/><line x1="30" y1="70" x2="14" y2="42"/><line x1="70" y1="70" x2="86" y2="42"/><line x1="50" y1="44" x2="24" y2="22"/><line x1="50" y1="44" x2="76" y2="22"/>
            <circle cx="50" cy="16" r="3" class="n"/><circle cx="14" cy="42" r="3" class="n"/><circle cx="86" cy="42" r="3" class="n"/><circle cx="24" cy="22" r="3" class="n"/><circle cx="76" cy="22" r="3" class="n"/>
            <circle cx="30" cy="70" r="5" class="n lit"/><circle cx="70" cy="70" r="5" class="n lit"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="5" class="n lit"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="way-copy">
            <span class="mono">Start on the strategy half</span>
            <h3>Top-down</h3>
            <p class="tag">A strategic foundation you expand on.</p>
            <p>You know something needs to change, not what is broken. Review the department, set the plan, then build out from it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 bottom-up: fix, build, scale ----->
    <section class="slide" data-name="Bottom-up">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">Bottom-up</p>
      <h2>Most people start with a project</h2>
      <div class="starts">
        <div class="start">
          <span class="mono">Something is broken</span>
          <h3>Fix it</h3>
          <p class="tag">Make what exists work better.</p>
          <p class="exlink"><em>Example</em> Event requests arriving by email, retyped by hand, now read and ticketed into Jira and Asana automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="start">
          <span class="mono">It does not exist yet</span>
          <h3>Build it</h3>
          <p class="tag">Make something new that needs to exist.</p>
          <p class="exlink"><em>Example</em> Google, LinkedIn, and Microsoft Ads connected to Claude, so the team asks for a budget shift and the same agent ships it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="start">
          <span class="mono">It works, by hand</span>
          <h3>Scale it</h3>
          <p class="tag">Make what works scale.</p>
          <p class="exlink"><em>Example</em> Two founders writing a weekly newsletter by hand, now reviewing a draft that research agents produce.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Execution first. It often grows into how we scale it and look at the whole.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 top-down: review the department -->
    <section class="slide" data-name="Top-down">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">Top-down &middot; 1 of 3</p>
      <h2>Review the department</h2>
      <p class="note intro">One function at a time. People, then process, then technology, measured against what the business needs most.</p>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="fnodes n3 chain lens">
          <div class="fnode l0"><b>People</b><small>Are the right people in the right seats, doing the right things consistently?</small></div>
          <button class="fnode l1" type="button" data-go="Process"><b>Process</b><small>Is the work written down, and does it run the same way every time?</small><span class="mono go">Process &rarr;</span></button>
          <button class="fnode l2" type="button" data-go="Technology and AI"><b>Technology</b><small>Can tools, automation, and AI make the process faster, bigger, and better?</small><span class="mono go">Technology &rarr;</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="outcomes">
          <span class="mono">Measured against</span>
          <div class="chips lit"><span>Increase revenue</span><span>Decrease cost</span><span>Reduce risk</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 top-down: process -->
    <section class="slide" data-name="Process">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">Top-down &middot; 2 of 3</p>
      <h2>Review it, document it, improve it</h2>
      <p class="note intro">If it is a process problem, I work with the founder and the department to walk the work as it is done today, write it down, and improve it until it holds.</p>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="fnodes n3 chain">
          <div class="fnode"><b>Review</b><small>Where it slows down, breaks, or depends on one person.</small></div>
          <div class="fnode"><b>Document</b><small>Steps, handoffs, owners, and the checks along the way.</small></div>
          <div class="fnode lit"><b>Improve</b><small>Cut steps, fix handoffs, add the checks that were missing.</small></div>
        </div>
        <div class="outcomes">
          <span class="mono">What you get</span>
          <div class="chips lit"><span>Process documentation</span><span>SOPs and checklists</span><span>Roles and owners</span><span>An improvement backlog</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 08 top-down: technology and AI -->
    <section class="slide" data-name="Technology and AI">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">Top-down &middot; 3 of 3</p>
      <h2>How I evaluate technology and AI</h2>
      <p class="note intro">Once the process is documented, four questions in order for each piece of it.</p>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="fnodes n4 chain">
          <div class="fnode"><b>Applications</b><small>Tools that do not exist today and should.</small></div>
          <div class="fnode"><b>Automations</b><small>What is already in place, made faster and more reliable.</small></div>
          <div class="fnode"><b>Assistance</b><small>AI in the work, with a person in the loop.</small></div>
          <div class="fnode"><b>Autonomous</b><small>AI end to end, inside clear bounds.</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Each one has to improve quality, time, scale, or efficiency, and serve more than one workflow.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 08 close: the site's intake form ---->
    <section class="slide" data-name="Work with me">
      <div class="close-grid">
        <div class="close-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow mono">Work with me</p>
          <h2>Tell me what is going on.</h2>
          <div class="seam" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="lede">Start with the thing that is costing you the most right now. I will read it today and reply within one business day.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="splash-btn primary print-cta" href="https://gregtoler.com/#contact">
              <span class="node-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span>
              <span>Start at gregtoler.com</span>
            </a>
            <a class="splash-btn ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gregtoler" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <span>Connect on LinkedIn</span>
              <svg class="ext" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7M9 7h8v8"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="v2 intake-host"><ContactIntake /></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- print only: the detail behind the clicks, as pages -->
    <section class="appendix" aria-label="Details">
      <div class="apage">
        <p class="eyebrow mono">The axes</p>
        <h2>How I think about the map</h2>
        <div class="acol">
          <h3>Strategy / Execution</h3>
          <p>Strategy is the top half. Deciding what to change and why. Which accounts, which processes, which systems, in what order. Execution is the bottom half. Doing the work. Building the tool, writing the automation, fixing the process, and handing it off so it runs without me. Most consultants do one or the other. I do both, so the plan and the build come from the same person.</p>
          <h3>GTM / Operations</h3>
          <p>Go-to-market is the left half. Anything that finds a buyer and moves them forward. Targeting, campaigns, content, paid media, sales follow-up. Operations is the right half. Anything that runs underneath. The CRM and its data, reporting, the systems that connect teams, automation and AI. Most problems sit on the line between the two. A pipeline problem is usually a process or tooling problem underneath, so I work both sides.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="apage">
        <p class="eyebrow mono">The four quadrants</p>
        <h2>What each one looks like</h2>
        <div class="aquads" id="aquads"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="apage">
        <p class="eyebrow mono">The pins, 1 of 2</p>
        <h2>Twelve examples, problem then build</h2>
        <p class="anote">Each one is written up in full at <a href="https://gregtoler.com/examples">gregtoler.com/examples</a>.</p>
        <div class="aex" id="aex1"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="apage">
        <p class="eyebrow mono">The pins, 2 of 2</p>
        <h2>Twelve examples, problem then build</h2>
        <p class="anote">Each one is written up in full at <a href="https://gregtoler.com/examples">gregtoler.com/examples</a>.</p>
        <div class="aex" id="aex2"></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <div class="keys mono" id="keys" aria-label="Slides"></div>
    <div class="nav">
      <a class="dl" id="dl" href="/overview/gt-strategies-deck.pdf" download>Download the PDF</a>
      <button type="button" id="prev" aria-label="Previous">&larr; Back</button>
      <button type="button" id="next" aria-label="Next">Next &rarr;</button>
    </div>
  </footer>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  /* the pins, verbatim from src/lib/examples.ts (the twelve the site pins) */
  const EX = [
    {q:"GTM, Strategy", x:.15, y:.20, t:"Account scoring and tiering", p:"Target lists were built by gut feel or by whichever vendor tag happened to be populated, and paid audiences inherited the same noise.", b:"A composite fit score across every account in the registry, rolled into four tiers with the features weighted in the open, so a rep can argue with a tier instead of a black box."},
    {q:"GTM, Strategy", x:.36, y:.36, t:"Competitive landing pages from closed-won data", p:"Paid search was bidding on competitor names and landing on the homepage. Comparison pages did not exist and the team disagreed about tone.", b:"Researched why deals were won against each competitor in the CRM, built three pages from that, and wired a CMS template so new variants are a prompt away, with the funnel tracked end to end."},
    {q:"GTM, Strategy", x:.30, y:.12, t:"Paid media inside Claude", p:"Multiple paid platforms, a team that was not technical enough to run them, and an agency being paid mostly to click buttons. Nobody could say what was live or pacing without waiting on a report.", b:"Three production MCP servers connect Google, LinkedIn, and Microsoft Ads to Claude, and a skill agent carries the ad playbooks and company context, so the team asks for a strategy or a budget shift and the same agent builds and deploys it."},
    {q:"Ops, Strategy", x:.62, y:.14, t:"Custom dashboards across systems that do not report together", p:"The CRM, the marketing automation tool, the sequencing tool, the phone system, and the work management tool each reported on themselves and none agreed on who had been contacted or which form fill became a meeting.", b:"Read only pulls from every source joined on the person and the account, then the dashboard the team actually needs built on that model, and finally the schema promoted to a hosted database so the full funnel reports without a script."},
    {q:"Ops, Strategy", x:.88, y:.34, t:"Metabase product data into HubSpot", p:"Product usage lived in the BI tool. The CRM got a hand built CSV once a week, so outreach, lifecycle emails, and account health all ran on stale data.", b:"Saved BI cards queried on a schedule and written to CRM properties on the contact and the company, matched on a user id so reruns update instead of duplicate, feeding trial scoring, lifecycle emails, and a paid health score."},
    {q:"Ops, Strategy", x:.66, y:.40, t:"Account health from Slack", p:"Checking an account's health meant a BI login and knowing the right saved question. Most people never looked.", b:"A Slack command takes an email or an org name, runs the same BI queries, and posts back a chart with a plain language summary and the score with the reasons behind it."},
    {q:"GTM, Execution", x:.13, y:.64, t:"Assessment chatbot into Marketo, Salesforce, and Lemlist", p:"A target list of 140 accounts needed a reason to engage beyond a whitepaper, and reps needed owned, warm leads without hand routing.", b:"A chatbot on the landing page adapts its questions as the visitor answers, turns the submission into a personalized audit, updates the marketing automation person, and in parallel routes the lead to an owner and enrolls it in that owner's sequence with copy drawn from the same answers."},
    {q:"GTM, Execution", x:.36, y:.84, t:"Content bot in Slack", p:"Marketing had produced hundreds of articles, guides, and videos. Sales could not find them, so they asked in Slack and waited, or sent nothing.", b:"A content repository indexed and wired to a retrieval layer and a model behind a Slack app. A rep asks a plain question and the bot answers from approved content and lists the exact pieces to share."},
    {q:"GTM, Execution", x:.16, y:.90, t:"Voice notes to CRM and drafted follow ups", p:"Event follow up died in the gap between the conversation and the laptop. Notes were lost, contacts never created, emails sent days late.", b:"A voice note from the phone is transcribed, matched to the event, written to the contact record, and turned into a personalized follow up waiting in the rep's drafts. Nothing sends without the rep."},
    {q:"Ops, Execution", x:.64, y:.62, t:"Event requests into Jira and Asana", p:"About ten event requests a week arrived by email in no fixed format. Every one had to be retyped into the ticketing system and chased for whatever was missing.", b:"A script watches a folder. Drop the email in and it reads the thread, creates the record and the tasks with eleven fields filled, asks the requester for anything missing, and updates only what changed when the answer comes back."},
    {q:"Ops, Execution", x:.88, y:.72, t:"Marketing requests into RevOps", p:"Marketing worked in Asana and RevOps worked in Jira. Requests were retyped by hand, half arrived without enough detail, and nobody could see progress once a ticket was in flight.", b:"Assigning a task hands it to an agent that pulls the full project context into a properly written ticket, sends a needs context subtask back when the detail is not there, and syncs status both ways after that."},
    {q:"Ops, Execution", x:.62, y:.90, t:"Research agents for a newsletter and tool directory", p:"Two founders were doing a weekly newsletter and a tool directory's research and writing by hand, which left little time for sales, customers, and events.", b:"A set of agents behind an orchestrator does the research and the writing at scale, with a quality gate, a hallucination check, and a newsletter draft waiting for approval. The founders review rather than write."}
  ];
  const SLUGS = ["account-scoring-and-tiering", "competitive-landing-pages-from-closed-won-data", "paid-media-inside-claude", "custom-dashboards-across-systems-that-do-not-report-together", "metabase-product-data-into-hubspot", "account-health-from-slack", "assessment-chatbot-into-marketo-salesforce-and-lemlist", "content-bot-in-slack", "voice-notes-to-crm-and-drafted-follow-ups", "event-requests-into-jira-and-asana", "marketing-requests-into-revops", "research-agents-for-a-newsletter-and-tool-directory"];
  const QUAD = {
    tl: { coord: "GTM, Strategy", title: "GTM strategy", lede: "Deciding who to sell to and how to reach them, with the data to back it. The target list, the positioning, and the channel plan, so the team is not guessing.",
          items: ["Account scoring, tiering, and target lists", "Positioning and competitive pages from closed-won evidence", "Paid media plans the team can actually run"] },
    tr: { coord: "Ops, Strategy", title: "RevOps & BizOps", lede: "Making the CRM, the marketing tools, and the product data agree, so the reporting is right and the team trusts the numbers it runs on.",
          items: ["CRM, marketing automation, and product data joined up", "Dashboards across tools that do not report together", "Account health, lifecycle, and pipeline reporting"] },
    bl: { coord: "GTM, Execution", title: "GTM execution", lede: "The campaigns, pages, content, and follow-up that reach a buyer, built so they work end to end and get measured.",
          items: ["Landing pages, chatbots, and lead routing that work end to end", "Content reps can find and send", "Event follow-up that happens the same day"] },
    br: { coord: "Ops, Execution", title: "Systems & automation", lede: "The plumbing underneath. Integrations, automation, agents, and internal tools, built to run without me and documented so the team owns them.",
          items: ["Requests moving between teams without retyping", "Agents that research, draft, and wait for approval", "Integrations, MCP servers, and custom internal tools"] }
  };

  const plane = document.getElementById('plane');
  function setMode(m) {
    plane.dataset.mode = m;
    plane.querySelectorAll('.axlab').forEach(a => a.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(m === a.dataset.axis)));
    if (m !== 'ex') plane.querySelectorAll('.pin').forEach(p => p.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'));
    if (m !== 'q') plane.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(n => n.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'));
  }
  function openEx(i, btn) {
    const e = EX[i];
    plane.querySelector('.ex-coord').textContent = e.q;
    plane.querySelector('.ex-title').textContent = e.t;
    plane.querySelector('.ex-problem').textContent = e.p;
    plane.querySelector('.ex-build').textContent = e.b;
    setMode('ex');
    plane.querySelectorAll('.pin').forEach(p => p.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(p === btn)));
  }
  function openQuad(key, btn) {
    const q = QUAD[key];
    plane.querySelector('.q-coord').textContent = q.coord;
    plane.querySelector('.q-title').textContent = q.title;
    plane.querySelector('.q-lede').textContent = q.lede;
    const ul = plane.querySelector('.q-list'); ul.innerHTML = '';
    q.items.forEach(t => { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = t; ul.appendChild(li); });
    setMode('q');
    plane.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(n => n.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(n === btn)));
  }
  const host = document.createElement('div');
  EX.forEach((e, i) => {
    const b = document.createElement('button');
    b.className = 'pin'; b.type = 'button';
    b.style.cssText = `left:${(e.x*100).toFixed(2)}%;top:${(e.y*100).toFixed(2)}%;--i:${i}`;
    b.setAttribute('aria-haspopup', 'dialog'); b.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    b.innerHTML = '<span class="ring" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="tip mono"></span>';
    b.querySelector('.tip').textContent = e.t;
    b.addEventListener('click', ev => { ev.stopPropagation(); openEx(i, b); });
    host.appendChild(b);
  });
  document.getElementById('pins').replaceWith(host);
  plane.querySelectorAll('.axlab').forEach(a => a.addEventListener('click', ev => { ev.stopPropagation(); setMode(plane.dataset.mode === a.dataset.axis ? 'grid' : a.dataset.axis); }));
  plane.querySelectorAll('.node').forEach(n => n.addEventListener('click', ev => { ev.stopPropagation(); openQuad(n.dataset.q, n); }));
  plane.querySelectorAll('.panel-close').forEach(c => c.addEventListener('click', ev => { ev.stopPropagation(); setMode('grid'); }));
  plane.querySelectorAll('.panel').forEach(p => p.addEventListener('click', ev => ev.stopPropagation()));
  plane.addEventListener('click', () => setMode('grid'));

  /* ---- print appendix content ---- */
  (() => {
    const aq = document.getElementById('aquads');
    Object.values(QUAD).forEach(q => {
      const d = document.createElement('div'); d.className = 'aquad';
      d.innerHTML = `<span class="mono"></span><h3></h3><p></p><ul></ul>`;
      d.querySelector('.mono').textContent = q.coord; d.querySelector('h3').textContent = q.title; d.querySelector('p').textContent = q.lede;
      q.items.forEach(t => { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = t; d.querySelector('ul').appendChild(li); });
      aq.appendChild(d);
    });
    EX.forEach((e, i) => {
      const ax = document.getElementById(i < 6 ? 'aex1' : 'aex2');
      const d = document.createElement('div'); d.className = 'aexi';
      d.innerHTML = `<span class="mono"></span><h3><a></a></h3><p><b>Problem.</b> <span class="p"></span></p><p><b>Build.</b> <span class="b"></span></p>`;
      d.querySelector('.mono').textContent = e.q;
      const a = d.querySelector('a'); a.textContent = e.t; a.href = 'https://gregtoler.com/examples#' + SLUGS[i];
      d.querySelector('.p').textContent = e.p; d.querySelector('.b').textContent = e.b;
      ax.appendChild(d);
    });
  })();

  /* ---- deck navigation ---- */
  const slides = [...document.querySelectorAll('.slide')];
  const keys = document.getElementById('keys');
  let cur = 0;
  slides.forEach((s, i) => {
    const k = document.createElement('button'); k.type = 'button'; k.textContent = String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0');
    k.setAttribute('aria-label', s.dataset.name); k.addEventListener('click', () => go(i));
    keys.appendChild(k);
  });
  function go(i) {
    if (typeof i === 'string') i = slides.findIndex(s => s.dataset.name === i);
    cur = Math.max(0, Math.min(slides.length - 1, i));
    slides.forEach((s, j) => s.classList.toggle('on', j === cur));
    keys.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((k, j) => k.classList.toggle('k-on', j === cur));
    document.getElementById('slide-name').textContent = slides[cur].dataset.name;
    document.getElementById('slide-count').textContent = `${cur + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
    setMode('grid');
  }
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-go]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => go(isNaN(+b.dataset.go) ? b.dataset.go : +b.dataset.go)));
  document.getElementById('next').addEventListener('click', () => go(cur + 1));
  document.getElementById('prev').addEventListener('click', () => go(cur - 1));
  document.addEventListener('keydown', ev => {
    if (ev.target.closest('input, textarea')) return;
    if (ev.key === 'ArrowRight' || ev.key === ' ' || ev.key === 'PageDown') { ev.preventDefault(); go(cur + 1); }
    else if (ev.key === 'ArrowLeft' || ev.key === 'PageUp') { ev.preventDefault(); go(cur - 1); }
    else if (ev.key === 'Escape') { setMode('grid'); }
    else if (ev.key === 'Home') { go(0); }
    else if (ev.key === 'End') { go(slides.length - 1); }
  });
  go(0);

</script>

  </body>
